From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:03:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 128/147] hjviewer: screen readers hear selections and state
 changes (UX-K2)

UX-K2 (U59, the part M2 does not do; M2 keeps the dialogs' reading
range):
- The PC list's tabs and the desktop settings' side bar rows are one
  node each, a button that says whether it is the selected one. The
  selected tab's name beside its icon no longer reads twice with its
  tooltip.
- The settings groups' titles are headings: the desktop settings'
  cards and the phone settings' sections.
- The selected PC list tab shows without its colour: the others take
  the outlined twin of their icon (recent, favourites, discovered,
  accessible devices); the address book's icon has none, so its
  selected pill draws a 2 px line under the icon.
- Live regions: the desktop's status line (Ready / not connected to
  the server), the notices above this PC's ID (P1, the P2 and P3
  ticket lines, G2) by their title or text, and G3. HjvCallout gains
  liveRegion (default off, which leaves its tree as it was). A live
  region is read again only when its text changes.
- The menus' current rows: the PC list's view and sort menus
  (RadioListTile) and the session toolbar's radio menus
  (RadioMenuButton) read as checked already; popup_menu.dart's
  check-mark radio rows, which the design named, have no user in the
  tree and stay as they are.

Test: flutter/test/hjviewer_semantics_test.dart (pure, no bridge).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
